| H4 | **NOT tested (P1): the real network's `HttpIOException`** (a subclass of `IOException` that `SocketsHttpHandler` raises when a connection ends mid-body) | a named limit: no catch in `ReadBoundedAsync` (`Oxpd2ClientCore.cs:72` to `:109` at BASE, DERIVED), so a subclass passes out the same way; the class name and when .NET raises it are UNMEASURED here (no socket in this lane) |
